attribution: Traditional American folk ballad from Appalachia, first recorded by Clarence Ashley in 1933 and sung by Georgia Turner to Alan Lomax in 1937; this is the plain traditional tune and the traditional words, not any later commercial arrangement, so both are public domain worldwide.
