# Verse 1
There is a house in New Or-leans
E4 A3(2) B3/ ~A3/ C4(2) D4 E4(2) C4/ ~B3/ A3(2)
they call the Ri-sing Sun.
E4 A4(2) E4 G4(2) E4/ ~D4/ E4(3) ~E4 r
It's been the ru-in of ma-ny a poor girl,
E4 A4(2) A3 C4 C4 D4 E4/ E4/ E4 C4/ ~B3/ A3(2)
and me, O God, for one.
E4 E4(2) E4 E4(2) C4/ ~B3/ A3(3) ~A3(2)

# Verse 2
My mo-ther, she's a tai-lor,
E4 A3(2) B3/ ~A3/ C4(2) D4 E4(2) C4/ ~B3/ ~A3(2)
she sewed those new blue jeans;
E4 A4(2) E4 G4(2) E4/ ~D4/ E4(3) ~E4 r
my sweet-heart, he's a drunk-ard, Lord,
E4 A4(2) A3 C4(2) D4 E4/ E4/ ~E4 C4/ ~B3/
Lord, drinks down in New Or-leans.
